"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[67487],{67487:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n\\n<center>\\n<MovieCard\\n  cover=\\"/assets/snippets/screen/3901608e62a06b4b883cd4e3cb546a13.jpg\\"\\n  title=\\"Spider-Man: Brand New Day (2026)\\"\\n  original_title=\\"Spider-Man: Brand New Day\\"\\n  release_date=\\"2026-07-28\\"\\n  runtime=\\"145\\"\\n  genres=[\\"SF\\"]\\n  rating=3.5\\n  tags=\\"movie\\"\\n/>\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nTo be honest, I haven\'t watched all of the <mark>Marvel series</mark>, so I can\'t say I watched this movie with a perfect understanding.  \\nStill, I did some previewing of the general context before going.  \\n\\nFortunately, it didn\'t seem to be heavily connected to the previous series.  \\nOf course, the catch is that I don\'t know enough to even distinguish what is connected and what is not.  \\nStill, I didn\'t have much trouble following the overall flow of the story.  \\n\\nFor your information, this movie also has a `post-credits scene`, which seemed like a major teaser for the subsequent series.  \\nBut, as expected, I don\'t know exactly what the situation is.  \\n\\nEvery time I watch a Marvel movie, I always think <mark>it would be nice to watch all the movies and drama series in order</mark>.  \\nBut there are so many series that I can\'t bring myself to do it.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nAfter watching, I also looked up other people\'s reviews, and the reception was surprisingly good.  \\n\\nLooking at the reviews, many said that <mark>Peter Parker has matured significantly</mark> in this installment.  \\nThey mentioned it portrayed him growing into an adult through loss and separation, departing from an immature hero. I also felt that the tone was definitely heavier than in the previous series.  \\n\\nI also learned for the first time that Destin Daniel Cretton, who directed `Shang-Chi`, was in charge of directing.  \\nPerhaps because of that, martial arts film-style slow-motion action sequences stood out in various places, and many reviews evaluated this part positively.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nHowever, some reviews pointed out that this movie felt more like a <mark>sketch for the next series</mark> rather than a complete story.  \\nSome described leaving the theater with a strange sense of emptiness, and I think I felt similarly while watching the post-credits scene.  \\nSince even someone like me who doesn\'t know much could feel that, it must have stood out even more to those who are well-informed.  "}')}}]);